### Extraction of GUS protein  
1. Preparation of Coomassie Brilliant Blue G250: Dissolve 100 mg of Coomassie Brilliant Blue G250 in 50 ml of 95% ethanol, add 100 μl of phosphoric acid, make up to 1 L in a volumetric flask, filter through a membrane, and store at 4°C;
2. Preparation of BSA standard curve: Prepare a 100 μg/ml BSA standard stock solution and dilute it to 7 concentration points of 0, 10, 20, 40, 60, 80, and 100 μg/ml;
3. Take 4 ml of each BSA concentration, add 1 ml of Coomassie Brilliant Blue, mix well, allow to stand at room temperature for 2 min, and measure the absorbance at 595 nm using the Infinite 200Pro multifunctional microplate reader;
4. Take 20 μl of the GUS extraction buffer from each sample, add water to 4 ml, then add 1 ml of Coomassie Brilliant Blue, mix well, and allow to stand at room temperature for 2 min;  
Measure the absorbance at 595 nm using the Infinite 200Pro multifunctional microplate reader, and calculate the protein concentration of the samples from the standard curve.

